{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1448888-time-management","id":1448888,"title":"Time Management.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-18T12:17:13-07:00","id":1448888,"title":"Time Management.","content":"So I'm wondering how others handle time management in MTA? And I mean more the abstract management of how much time characters spend on any one thing, not managing the sphere of Time.<br /> <br /> I feel like in part, nitpicking seconds or individual minutes could be frustrating for everyone, but I think time-blocs of 10 minutes or so is decent for crunch time, and hours for more casual moments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T15:51:50-07:00","id":1448905,"title":"","content":"Are we talking broadly over the course of a chronicle or during combat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T06:32:30-07:00","id":1448976,"title":"","content":"I mean in broad terms. Mage is a game that can easily get out of hand if you don't keep close track of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T16:17:48-07:00","id":1449056,"title":"","content":"That...is going to depend on a lot of things, and in what context.<br /> <br /> Do you mean in terms of ritual Effects? Crafting? Legwork rolls? Scene/Story/Chronicle progression? Something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T06:03:45-07:00","id":1449107,"title":"","content":"Well, my basic thoughts are each day involves roughly 10 hours of downtime at minimum. 8 hours of sleep, 2 hours of eating/hygiene.<br /> <br /> This leaves 14 hours a day. Minus however much time the characters spend at any jobs or chantry duties they might have.<br /> <br /> So, from there we work out a rough daily schedule of each character, and we work around that hour by hour, leaving a few blocks of time, doing our best to ensure they get at least one synchronized block of time for adventuring &amp; mage shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T14:31:35-07:00","id":1449209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1448888-time-management?p=1449107#post1449107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, my basic thoughts are each day involves roughly 10 hours of downtime at minimum. 8 hours of sleep, 2 hours of eating/hygiene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't it get reduced to 4-6 hours of sleep? Even assuming it is detrimental to health in the long-term, Mages have Life Magick to compensate. And I can imagine Mind, Life or Prime Effects that make full rest with less sleep possible.<br /> 2 hours of eating and hygiene? Can't they quickly munch on some fast food? Or buy frozen dinners, and eat them quickly? If they insist on homemade food, then they can cook in bulk or have Acolytes do it. And take quick showers.<br /> Mages have such important and varied priorities and goals that even a few extra hours might make all the difference; it adds up over an entire week or a month. Hence I can very much see them cutting down on fulfilling basic needs. It is kind of funny to consider Mages being like &quot;have to eat a proper breakfast and at least three meals per day&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-22-2021, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T06:02:10-07:00","id":1449241,"title":"","content":"This strikes me as too granular. There\u2019s a lot of stuff that goes on in a Mage\u2019s life (focus preparation, socialization, dinner) that doesn\u2019t need to be \u2018on screen\u2019 unless it is important. You don\u2019t really need to be worried about time intervals until then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T08:03:22-07:00","id":1449250,"title":"","content":"Yeah, to me it's not really necessary to be this simulationist with Mage.<br /> <br /> Nvm that WoD's systems in general aren't really suited to be simulationist without rewriting the systems from the ground up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T08:20:49-07:00","id":1449251,"title":"","content":"For me time meets the needs of the story. If there is a time limit them monitor time, otherwise it is a narrative rather than a detailed thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T08:29:31-07:00","id":1449255,"title":"","content":"As I mentioned in another thread, time in World of Darkness games gets measured in scenes, stories, and chronicles. The closest thing I've seen to time management as I understand the request is something that I vaguely recall seeing in the Transylvania chronicle, which was designed to bridge Vampire the Dark Ages to Vampire the Masquerade and had mechanisms for lengthy periods of downtime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T09:12:37-07:00","id":1449261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1448888-time-management?p=1449255#post1449255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned in another thread, time in World of Darkness games gets measured in scenes, stories, and chronicles. The closest thing I've seen to time management as I understand the request is something that I vaguely recall seeing in the Transylvania chronicle, which was designed to bridge Vampire the Dark Ages to Vampire the Masquerade and had mechanisms for lengthy periods of downtime.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was also a seasonal experience system in some mage source book I think? Somewhere around Revised?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I agree that this is too over detailed for my taste. It might be helpful to have a sense of characters daily routines, especially if maintaining those routines is part of their paradigm (is, daily prayers or meditation). But I don't need to know what's happening every 10 minute block.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24383-laughinggull","name":"LaughingGull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T09:40:31-07:00","id":1449264,"title":"","content":"You're right. I think it was in the storytellers handbook.<br /> <br /> And yeah, even GURPS only went with hour by hour for its time management system. And it's a system that most gaming groups steer clear of if they can help it. If it's too simulationist for GURPS\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T06:32:58-07:00","id":1449547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1448888-time-management?p=1449209#post1449209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't it get reduced to 4-6 hours of sleep? Even assuming it is detrimental to health in the long-term, Mages have Life Magick to compensate. And I can imagine Mind, Life or Prime Effects that make full rest with less sleep possible.<br /> 2 hours of eating and hygiene? Can't they quickly munch on some fast food? Or buy frozen dinners, and eat them quickly? If they insist on homemade food, then they can cook in bulk or have Acolytes do it. And take quick showers.<br /> Mages have such important and varied priorities and goals that even a few extra hours might make all the difference; it adds up over an entire week or a month. Hence I can very much see them cutting down on fulfilling basic needs. It is kind of funny to consider Mages being like &amp;quot;have to eat a proper breakfast and at least three meals per day&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly it could be reduced, but the combined 10 hours of downtime is going to be standard without some kind of action taken to make more time. Magical actions have obvious costs, but just neglecting to take care of yourself has its costs as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1448888-time-management?p=1449241#post1449241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This strikes me as too granular. There\u2019s a lot of stuff that goes on in a Mage\u2019s life (focus preparation, socialization, dinner) that doesn\u2019t need to be \u2018on screen\u2019 unless it is important. You don\u2019t really need to be worried about time intervals until then.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The idea isn't that each block of time needs to be on screen. It's more to figure out a schedule, so we know what the scenes will be. We don't need to make a scene of every bit of downtime, or prepwork, but having an idea of what characters do with their time is important.<br /> <br /> For example we don't need a scene of each of them sitting in traffic. We do need to make a scene of their investigation of the murder that's after the sitting in traffic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1448888-time-management?p=1449255#post1449255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned in another thread, time in World of Darkness games gets measured in scenes, stories, and chronicles. The closest thing I've seen to time management as I understand the request is something that I vaguely recall seeing in the Transylvania chronicle, which was designed to bridge Vampire the Dark Ages to Vampire the Masquerade and had mechanisms for lengthy periods of downtime.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be honest though, they're kind of shit at certain things. Time Management is one of them. It's why making artifacts is so absurdly overpowered in Forged by Dragons Fire. Because the assumption was you were basically skipping out on a session to forge this thing, it had better be worth it.<br /> <br /> While the scene, story measure is relevant, I don't think it's an adequate replacement for actually tracking time. And likewise, you don't necessarily need to track all of everyone's time, all the time. But given mages ability to stockpile resources, Time management and ensuring those resources are spent before they snowball is an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}